{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"C3c CLOSED (Gerrit 1889 green; completion-verifier passed). C3d (Gerrit 1890): impl landed, held-out oracle GREEN+teeth, plan re-review PASS+signed, CLOSE-valid=certified, AC ticked — blocked on close only by 1890 Verified pending (CI running).\n\nLESSONS (require_plan_review_for_close=True): (1) CLOSE profile tolerates CODE drift but NOT material edits (file_impact+description; ticking AC [ ]->[x] is attestation-safe). Editing file_impact after PASS stales CLOSE -> forces re-review. (2) Re-review P4 gate = 8000-char desc limit; COMPRESS. E4/G1G2 grounding reads a BASE sha not HEAD: slice whose commit is an ANCESTOR (C3c) shows rows GONE -> add short end-state note; slice that IS HEAD (C3d) shows rows PRESENT -> keep FORWARD-LOOKING (no 'already done' banner). (3) RIGHT ORDER (avoid churn): finalize complete predicted file_impact (superset OK) + final desc (<8000, forward-looking, AC unchecked) BEFORE locking review -> PASS -> claim -> implement exact files -> commit -> push -> tick AC -> close after Verified+1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787115532304661001,"uuid":"fe6f7a7a-d585-42c8-aa13-d0ce7f2ce701"}